Review of PR #2426 is done: 10 findings, all posted as inline comments on the PR. None were verified by running code (this review level has no verify pass); they come from reading the diff and its callers. Three comments are anchored to the nearest line inside a diff hunk because the defect line itself is unchanged code: the `suite_io_service.py` 526 and 80 findings sit on lines 508 and 303, and the `_check_diff` finding sits on `coverage_settings_service.py` 407.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/suite_io_service.py",
    "line": 526,
    "summary": "apply_document strips inherit_coverage_settings on the create branch but not the update branch, and validate_document never checks it, so a document can be refused mid-loop after earlier writes committed.",
    "failure_scenario": "Apply an exported automatic suite's document onto an ordinary suite that already has a same-named check: update_check -> settle_edit raises InheritEditError (not a baseline, flag sent) -> 422 inside the write loop, after earlier creates/updates each committed. The dry-run plan showed a clean 'update'. Same partial apply on the automatic suite itself when the document carries true plus a changed threshold."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/api/v1/checks.py",
    "line": 145,
    "summary": "REST and MCP reads return inherit_coverage_settings: true inside config, so a read-modify-write that changes a threshold or the window is refused instead of pinning the check.",
    "failure_scenario": "A client GETs an inheriting check, changes window 8 -> 14, and PATCHes the whole config back (required, since config is replaced wholesale). settle_edit sees true plus a changed value and returns 422. Only the UI escapes, because formToConfig rebuilds config from spec fields and drops the key."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/coverage_settings_service.py",
    "line": 373,
    "summary": "On a pinned check, inherit_coverage_settings: true sent together with changed thresholds is accepted and the thresholds are silently discarded; the 'true with a changed value is refused' rule only runs on the inheriting branch.",
    "failure_scenario": "Pinned check with warn 5; PATCH {config: {..., inherit_coverage_settings: true}, warn_threshold: 2}. Stored warn becomes 2, the flag flips to true, every run bands at the effective value (e.g. 3), and the response shows 3. The caller's 2 is never used and nothing reports that."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/coverage_settings_service.py",
    "line": 377,
    "summary": "A shape key omitted from a replacement config means 'keep' on an inheriting check but 'default' on a pinned one, so an edit made by omission is silently ignored.",
    "failure_scenario": "Inheriting check with seasonality true in effect; a caller (e.g. an LLM told config is assigned wholesale) sends {target_metric, window, min_points} to switch seasonality off. sent_shape lacks the key, nothing counts as changed, and the check stays inheriting and seasonal with a 200. The same payload on a pinned check does switch it off. A test pins this as intended, so it may be a deliberate trade-off."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/suite_io_service.py",
    "line": 372,
    "summary": "_check_diff compares the document against the stored snapshot and flag, so a document holding the effective values (or an older flagless export) never converges under apply.",
    "failure_scenario": "A GitOps file for an automatic suite contains what the REST read shows (effective 5/6/7; stored snapshot 3/4/6). Every apply plans 'update', calls update_check, settle_edit keeps the stored snapshot, and a new check_versions row and audit event are written each time with nothing changed."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/suite_io_service.py",
    "line": 80,
    "summary": "export_suite (REST and MCP) still emits the stored creation-time snapshot for an inheriting check, and import strips the flag, so the imported check is pinned at values the source no longer ran on.",
    "failure_scenario": "Workspace setting moved 3/4/6 -> 5/6/7 after the check was created. Export says 3/4/6 with the flag true; import strips the flag; the new suite's check alerts at 3/4/6. MCP export_suite returns the same numbers with no caveat."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/datasources/monitors.py",
    "line": 348,
    "summary": "retain_seasonal_horizon protects history across a seasonality switch but not across a window change, so lowering the inherited window trims every inheriting check's baseline.",
    "failure_scenario": "Admin lowers the workspace window 8 -> 2: on the next run each inheriting check is trimmed to 14 observations. Raising it back to 8 leaves seasonal checks in cold start (skip) for weeks, across the whole workspace, from one settings edit."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/api/v1/checks.py",
    "line": 139,
    "summary": "Reuse: the overlay of effective config, thresholds and level onto a check is written twice, in _read_all and in mcp/server.py _check_summary.",
    "failure_scenario": "Two hand-written copies of 'what this check runs on' can drift (export already shows a third answer). One CheckSettings.overlay(check) or service-level effective view would serve REST, MCP and export."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/mcp/server.py",
    "line": 1049,
    "summary": "Simplification: a one-element 'for inherited in [...]' loop is used as a let-binding in a comprehension; _inherited is a pass-through; _settle_inheritance builds a throwaway SuiteCoverage(resolve(None)) for every non-automatic check.",
    "failure_scenario": "Harder to read and maintain. Bind page and inherited above the return, and let settle_edit accept coverage=None for checks that cannot inherit."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/coverage_service.py",
    "line": 214,
    "summary": "Efficiency: _ensure_checks resolves for_suite (workspace row plus asset read) on every reconcile pass for every covered suite, though it is only needed when a baseline role is missing.",
    "failure_scenario": "After the first pass no roles are missing, yet each sweep still pays the settings resolution per suite. Resolve it lazily inside add_baseline."
  }
]
```

No CLAUDE.md convention violations were found that could be quoted rule-against-line.

